# Image & Asset Management Rules

## 🖼️ Asset Management Patterns

### Image Upload Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - S3 upload with presigned URL
const uploadImageToS3 = async (file: File) => {
  // 1. Get presigned URL
  const presignedUrl = await fetchPresignedUrl({
    fileName: file.name,
    fileType: file.type,
  });

  // 2. Upload to S3
  const uploadResponse = await fetch(presignedUrl.uploadUrl, {
    method: "PUT",
    body: file,
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": file.type,
    },
  });

  return presignedUrl.fileUrl;
};
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** use presigned URLs for S3 uploads
✅ **ALWAYS** validate image file types and sizes
✅ **ALWAYS** implement proper error handling for uploads
✅ **ALWAYS** use appropriate image formats (WebP, PNG, JPG)
✅ **ALWAYS** implement lazy loading for images
✅ **ALWAYS** provide alt text for accessibility
✅ **ALWAYS** optimize images before upload

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** upload files directly to S3 without presigned URLs
❌ **NEVER** forget to validate file types
❌ **NEVER** upload files without size limits
❌ **NEVER** forget to handle upload errors
❌ **NEVER** use images without alt text
❌ **NEVER** forget to optimize images

### Image Processing Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Image processing utility
const processNewImage = async (file: File) => {
  // 1. Validate file
  const fileInfo = getFileInfo(file);
  if (!isValidImageType(fileInfo.type)) {
    throw new Error("Invalid image type");
  }

  // 2. Get image metadata
  const metadata = await getImageMeta(file);

  // 3. Upload to S3
  const imageUrl = await uploadImageToS3(file);

  return {
    url: imageUrl,
    metadata,
    fileInfo,
  };
};
```

### SVG Usage Pattern

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - SVG component usage
import { ReactComponent as Logo } from "@assets/image/logo.svg";

function Header() {
  return (
    <header>
      <Logo width={120} height={40} />
    </header>
  );
}

// ✅ CORRECT - SVG as background
const IconButton = styled.button`
  background-image: url(${({ theme }) => theme.assets.iconArrow});
  background-size: contain;
  background-repeat: no-repeat;
  width: 2.4rem;
  height: 2.4rem;
`;
```

